"The portal is somewhere on the level" isn't going to get you through
Fire and Air, which are the two Planes from which it's most necessary
to escape quickly.  Well, fine, that doesn't count Astral.  Anyway, you
need a method for finding portals.  Practically, that means either a
crystal ball (which only barely counts because it's a *pain*) or
non-cursed scrolls of gold detection.  Make sure you've got 4 of these
before you start the endgame, and then on each plane cast some spell
you've forgotten until you're confused but not stunned, and the portal
will reveal itself.  Then you're free to use your unicorn horn and zip
over there at top speed.  As I mentioned, this method helps a lot on
Earth and Water, but on Air if you don't get outta there quick you're
going to get pulped by the hyper-powered air elementals, and on Fire
the hordes summoned by the resident Archons will kill you almost as
fast.

Keep your ring of levitation on from before you step on the portal into
Air until you're on Astral.  Obviously it's a necessity on Air.
Without it you have to go around the lava pits instead of over them on
Fire.  If you don't have either it or an amulet of magical breathing
for Water (or levitation from some other source, I guess) then you have
to wait forever or until your bubble merges with the one with the
portal, whichever comes first (and in my experience, that's usually
'forever').  As soon as you step onto Astral, though, take off the
=oLevitation and put on Conflict.  (I assume your other finger has been
taken up by a =oFree Action through all of this, right?)  I'm not
completely sure what this will do as far as the guardian / nemesis
angel(s) situation, but it doesn't matter; you'd rather have to face a
mob plus a few angels with conflict than a mob without conflict, even
if you do get a pet that's irrelevant to this fast-moving stage of the
game with the second option.

> Astral - make sure i get the Angel pet (guess I need to #offer stuff at
> the last alter before leaving the dungeon).  Hope I avoid Death,
> Famine, and Pestilence.  I'm pretty sure I need more info on this one
> too..

You can't avoid all 3; there's one standing in front of each altar.
You should bring the necessary supplies for encounters with each (you
should have dropped most of your food by now but keep some K-rations
for Pestilence; a blessed unicorn horn will get you through against
Pestilence; and, um, crossed fingers and distance attacks will do best
vs. Death).  Your basic gameplan vs. these guys should be: 1) give them
the finger as soon as you can see them, unless it's Death (in which
case substitute Magic Missile), and if necessary 2) Whack them with one
of the 5 or so blessed potions of paralysis which I hope you remembered
to take with you (always assuming, of course, that you're wearing the
=oFA I told you to wear), followed by 3) beat them to death if you
want, or you could just leave them there for close to the same effect
(since if they die they'll resurrect so either way will incapacitate
them only temporarily anyway and you'll still have to face them again
on your way out of the altar room if it's the wrong one, either way you
do it.

> Most importantly I have a wand of wishing with three charges.

Feeling lazy?  You could always wish for a couple of the things I
mentioned above (specifically, an uncursed magic marker would be great
for writing those 4 uncursed ?oGD, which are a pain to find otherwise).
 However, it's also nice to keep a wish or two in reserve for
emergencies, especially on your first ascension run (since you're more
likely than more experienced players to only figure out at the last
second how screwed you're about to be).  Cockatrice corpses are good
ways to get out of hard fights, but you should only wish for one if you
really are going to have a hard time otherwise (keep in mind that that
shouldn't really happen to an endgame Wizard; they're really, really
powerful.  Also keep in mind that if necessary, you can always drop the
Amulet (just don't do it while levitating) and fire off some spells
without the extra MP cost, then pick it back up again once you've given
that mob the finger and continue on your quest.
 
